<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill picks European stocks.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill picks European stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strategists at Merrill Lynch named eight continental European stocks, one Israeli and one South African stock that they expect to outperform through 1997, market sources said.</p>
<p>The 10 stocks were SGS-Thomson,  Zurich Insurance, Credit Commercial de France, Veba, Henkel, Stet, Novartis, Gucci and Israel's Biotech General.</p>
<p>Merrill also said South Africa's Absa was also likely to outperform next year.</p>
<p>The list was presented as part of a global portfolio of stocks which Merrill strategists expect to outperform next year.</p>
<p>Strategist David Bowers at the brokerage said he expected monetary policy in continental Europe to remain soft amid tepid economic growth, and that interest-rate sensitive and &quot;growth&quot; stocks were likely to outperform in this environment.</p>
<p>However, he said investors should watch for a recovery in the pace of economic growth which would make cyclical stocks Bowers said he expects markets in Spain, Switzerland and France to outperform in the year ahead, and suggested investors should underweight the more growth-sensitive markets of Germany and Sweden.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
